  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"17a\"><p><strong>17a</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Rearranging the diffraction grating equation:</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{sin \\theta} = \\frac{d}{n \\lambda}\"></span></p>\n<p>Using any point from the graph <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"(\"></span>here I use <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"(2,1.06))\"></span>:</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.06 = \\frac{2 \\times 10^{-6}}{3 \\lambda}\"></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda \\approx 6.29 \\times 10^{-7}\"></span> m</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f = \\frac{3 \\times 10^{8}}{6.29 \\times 10^{-7}} \\approx 4.8 \\times 10^{14}\"></span> Hz</p>\n<p></p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"17b\"><p><strong>17b</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>The grating has many more slits, so the fringes in the second pattern are much narrower.</p>\n<p>The slits in the grating are much narrower, so the intensity of the fringes in the second pattern is constant.</p>\n<p>More light passes through the grating, so the peaks in the second pattern are higher.</p>\n<p>The distance between the slits in the grating is much smaller, so the maxima in the second pattern are farther apart.</p>\n<p></p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Monochromatic light is incident on a diffraction grating. The distance between adjacent slits in the grating is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"D\"></span> and the angle between the straight-through position and the third-order diffraction maximum is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta\"></span>. The graph shows how <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{sin \\theta}\"></span> varies with <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"D\"></span>.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>a. Determine the frequency of the incident light.</p>\n<p>  [3]</p>\n<p>The diagrams show interference patterns for a double-slit and a diffraction grating.</p>\n<p>Double-slit:</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure>\n\n<p>Diffraction grating:</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_03\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 3\" src=\"asset:fig_03\"/></figure>\n\n<p>b. State and explain the differences between the two patterns.</p>\n<p>  [3]</p>"
  },
